    "_conformed_basis_note": "Interactive Brokers recategorised the components of net interest income twice and conformed prior periods in later releases: the 2Q2018 and 4Q2018 EX-99.1s moved negative-interest-rate currency components into 'Customer credit balances, net', and the 3Q2018 EX-99.1 moved U.S. Treasury and reverse-repo components into 'Other net interest income, net'. Until 2026-08-31 this page carried the ORIGINAL figures for the affected quarters and the conformed ones after, so the segregated-funds yield line joined two categorisations at 2018Q2/2018Q3 and average interest-earning assets joined two at 2017Q4/2018Q1, where the 'FDIC sweeps' component enters. Nothing caught it because the recategorisations move dollars BETWEEN components: total net interest income and the overall margin are the same on both bases, so every sum on this page held. The six yield quarters 2017Q1-2018Q2, the four 2017 asset quarters and 2017Q4's margin now carry the conformed figure, each read from the release one year later that reprints it as a prior-year comparative.",
    "_2016_not_confirmed_note": "The four 2016 quarters are NOT confirmed on the conformed basis, and this page cannot confirm them: IBKR's EX-99.1 NET INTEREST MARGIN table did not exist before the 3Q2017 release, so no document reprints 2016 after either recategorisation. There is evidence they may need no change -- the 3Q2018 footnote names the affected quarters explicitly as 1Q2017 through 2Q2018, which excludes 2016 -- but that is the company describing one of the two changes, not a reprint of the numbers. So these four cells are the original figures, kept rather than nulled, with the boundary stated here instead of being left to look continuous. Whoever finds a 2016 reprint should replace them or confirm them."
  },
